// t-parser-a-04: `#[attr]` above a positional call argument is a parse error
// command: graphix --check design/review-2026-10-12/repro/t-parser-a-04.gx
// expected: parses and checks, as `f(#x: #[native] 1 + 2)` (labeled),
//   `[#[native] 1 + 2]` (array element) and a `//` comment above a
//   positional argument all do.
// observed: "Parse error at line: 11, column: 2 / Unexpected `(` /
//   Expected whitespace or end of input"; with a preceding argument,
//   `f(1, #[native] 1 + 2)`, "the parser could not continue past this point"
//   at the `(`.
let f = |x| x + 1;
f(#[native] 1 + 2)
